## Polish-round review: decisions and additions

- `shared_blobs.source`: `'seed'` only for the embedded fallback; blobs produced by publishing the Jig part are `'runtime'`.
- Parts link the `jig.css` hash recorded at build time (content-addressed, immutable, reproducible) and pick up a new Jig with `part_edit {rebuild: true}`, the same rule as the library set (T60/T61).
- The `code` viewer shell (T118) shares `pf-shell.css`, so the swap to `jig.css` covers `markdown`, `text` and `code`.
- Test added: `pf_ops::design_system::tests::rules_and_starter_come_from_live_version_not_head` (a broken Jig head never changes the op output).
- Split into T54.a / T54.b / T54.c (see the subtasks); this parent is the integration/closure bead.

